{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Let there be a rakia in the midst of the waters.</b> Let there be a nature within the elemental waters — like a sphere revolving within them — separating some of them from others in form, so that a certain upper portion of the waters, toward the air, reverts to a vaporous nature. Through this they necessarily rose to a certain boundary in the elemental air, and the air necessarily received a certain compression, to make room for the portion that had turned to vapor and expanded into a region of greater quantity than its first place."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:11:20.225370182Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}